# 16. TYPOGRAPHY

Use a modern sans-serif font family.

Recommended options:
- Inter.
- Manrope.
- Space Grotesk.

Use one primary font family and, optionally, a complementary heading font.

Suggested hierarchy:

Hero name:
64–88px on large desktop screens.

Section headings:
36–48px.

Project titles:
22–28px.

Body text:
15–18px.

Navigation:
12–14px.

Small metadata:
12–13px.

Use responsive typography with CSS clamp().

Example:

font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 5.5rem);

Use bold weights for important headings and regular weights for body text.

Maintain appropriate line height and paragraph spacing.

Avoid using too many font weights or decorative fonts.

Ensure that headings remain readable on mobile devices.

